  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU administration fee on administration of delegated partnership on support to Legal Service Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Governance and Rights Programme 2016-21 will contribute to the promotion of democracy, good governance, rule of law and respect for human rights with a special focus on women. 
 The theory of change  for the programme is based on the assumption that democratic, transparent and accountable governance where women&#x2019;s rights are equal to men&#x2019;s provides the most fertile ground for economic development and eradication of poverty and inequality. Strengthening of demand-side governance will contribute to stronger institutional checks and balances, empower citizens, and enhance the potential impact of Danish support provided to Government. In the short-term, change is expected in terms of a stronger and more vocal civil society, increasingly demanding transparency and responsive governance from duty bearers, as well as an increased access to justice for women and men. A particular change is expected in terms of increased awareness of and respect for women&#x2019;s rights.</narrative>
  </description>
